---
title: Proposed Forge worker and main-thread ownership
---
flowchart TB
    subgraph Browser["Browser execution contexts"]
        Main["Main JS thread<br/>Capture actions and render Canvas or DOM"]
        ViewBridge(["Actions and frame time to Rust<br/>Committed views to JS"])
        Runtime["Rust main thread<br/>Own policy, fixed ticks, assets and replay"]
        Effects(["Typed work requests to JS<br/>Correlated results to Rust"])
        Support["JS support workers<br/>Run requested I/O or computations"]
        Compute["Rust support backend<br/>Run independent compute when configured"]
        Main <--> ViewBridge <--> Runtime
        Runtime <--> Effects <--> Support
        Support -. Relay committed views .-> Main
        Support <--> Compute
    end
    subgraph Services[" "]
        Host["Studio service boundary<br/>Forge host admits commands and queues builds"]
        Queue["PostgreSQL<br/>Persist Studio jobs, leases and events"]
        Builder["Native Studio build worker<br/>Claim leases and execute pinned builds<br/>Resolve worker-scoped providers"]
        Artifacts["Artifact store<br/>Immutable bytes by digest"]
        Host <--> Queue
        Queue <--> Builder
        Builder --> Artifacts
    end
    Support <--> Host
